# D19 decision (Astra for the orchestrator, 2026-10-18): tests/test_perch.py

Decision: LAND

- `tests/test_perch.py`: Replaces assertions endorsing the deleted completion hook with installed-client review/recovery checks, exact evidence and recovery-pin assertions, and checks prohibiting direct completion (`tests/test_perch.py:1936`, `tests/test_perch.py:1949`, `tests/test_perch.py:1980`, `tests/test_perch.py:2007`). This follows the row’s requirement that completion and recovery use owner-started manager turns (`projects/program/tasklist.md:208`; `ops/bootstrap/perch_fake_claude.py:118`). Doctored-evidence cases strengthen protection: missing manager turns, direct completion, incorrect citations, unresolved holds and absent recovery dispositions must fail (`tests/test_perch.py:1061`, `tests/test_perch.py:1082`). The missing-landing mutation again runs inside the test whose final-status snapshot was deleted, preserving detection of suppressed Store-event diagnostics (`tests/test_perch.py:1048`, `tests/test_perch.py:1055`). The binding timer correction is satisfied: manager commands have no timeout and waits use state-based polling without deadlines (`ops/bootstrap/perch_fake_claude.py:106`, `ops/bootstrap/perch_fake_claude.py:181`, `ops/bootstrap/perch.sh:598`; `ops/requests.md:1612`). Patch-scan scope remains unchanged as directed.